      "dom_id": "step-q118706",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14247051/assets/1b3636b4a0534a8794c7b7955aa16d8bb90d98dcdaebbc40311c2e13e971e7af.png)\n\nGiven $△PQR$ shown above, which of the following diagrams represents the height corresponding to $\\overset{―}{PR}?$",
      "worked_solution": "The height (or altitude) corresponding to $\\overset{―}{PR}$ is a line segment that \n\n- runs from the opposite vertex $Q$ to the line $\\overset{⟷}{PR},$ and\n\n- is perpendicular to $\\overset{⟷}{PR}.$\n\nTo draw the height, we proceed as follows:\n\n- Extend the line segment $\\overset{―}{PR}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14247051/assets/94e65bdbb5e82c72b97f69ab2da1b16e2efe8399a83e78a2721d1e74eaa9b8b4.png)\n\n- Draw the perpendicular from $Q$ to $\\overset{⟷}{PR}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14247051/assets/aa3254d24cd0d21a8a78009c8c07591e34ab46fa0449fc27e179d5a32ac70a17.png)",
